WEBVTT


00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.007
It's time
to get out.


00:07:39.691 --> 00:07:41.591
Don't bleed
to death.


00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:48.099
- Hello, Mitchell.
- Bond.


00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.725
The Americans are gonna be
none too pleased about this.


00:07:50.802 --> 00:07:52.770
I promised them Le Chiffre,
and they got Le Chiffre.


00:07:52.871 --> 00:07:54.270
They got his body.


00:07:54.372 --> 00:07:58.433
If they'd wanted his soul, they should
have made a deal with a priest.


00:07:58.543 --> 00:08:00.909
- Has he said anything?
- No.


00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:03.812
I'm going to check the perimeter, ma'am.


00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.542
You look like hell.


00:08:06.618 --> 00:08:08.916
When's the last time you slept?


00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.886
Vesper's boyfriend, Yusef Kabira,


00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:15.222
the one who was abducted in Morocco,
the one she was trying to save.


00:08:15.293 --> 00:08:17.625
His body was washed up
on a beach in Ibiza.


00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:20.391
We're meant to believe
the fish did that to his face.


00:08:20.465 --> 00:08:22.262
His wallet and ID were in his pocket.


00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.063
- Well, that's convenient.
- Quite.


00:08:24.135 --> 00:08:28.299
Which is why I did a DNA check on a lock
of his hair found in Vesper's apartment.


00:08:28.406 --> 00:08:29.464
It's not him.


00:08:29.574 --> 00:08:31.269
A lock of his hair?


00:08:31.343 --> 00:08:34.141
I wouldn't have thought
Vesper the sentimental type.


00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.806
Well, we never really know anyone,
do we?


00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:40.644
But I do need to know, Bond.


00:08:41.019 --> 00:08:43.647
I need to know that I can trust you.


00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:45.581
And you don't?


00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:47.022
Well, it'd be a pretty cold bastard


00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:49.992
who didn't want revenge
for the death of someone he loved.


00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:52.154
You don't have to worry about me.


00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:55.495
I'm not gonna go chasing him.
He's not important.


00:08:57.769 --> 00:08:59.498
And neither was she.


00:09:00.505 --> 00:09:01.836
It's clear, ma'am.


00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.170
- Thanks, Mitchell.
- Shall we?


00:09:23.361 --> 00:09:25.989
Are you gonna tell us who you work for?


00:09:26.064 --> 00:09:29.295
I was always very interested to meet you.


00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:31.733
I'd heard so much about you from Vesper.


00:09:31.836 --> 00:09:34.964
The real shame is that
if she hadn't killed herself,


00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.974
we would have had you, too.


00:09:37.042 --> 00:09:40.375
I think you would have done
anything for her.


00:09:40.478 --> 00:09:43.970
Well, you know you're not in Britain,
and God knows where you'll be tomorrow.


00:09:44.049 --> 00:09:45.482
Which should tell you that eventually


00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:48.678
you will tell us about
the people you work with,


00:09:48.753 --> 00:09:52.348
and the longer it takes,
the more painful we'll make it.


00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:57.560
You really don't know anything about us.


00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:05.200
It's so amusing because
we are on the other side, thinking,


00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:08.000
"The Ml6, the CIA,
they're looking over our shoulders.


00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:09.870
"They're listening to our conversations."


00:10:09.941 --> 00:10:13.069
And the truth is
you don't even know we exist.


00:10:13.178 --> 00:10:16.614
Well, we do now, Mr. White,
and we're quick learners.


00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:19.673
Oh, really?


00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:22.949
Well, then, the first thing
you should know about us


00:10:23.054 --> 00:10:25.545
is that we have people everywhere.


00:10:26.391 --> 00:10:27.756
Am I right?


00:15:42.373 --> 00:15:43.704
Anything?


00:15:44.709 --> 00:15:47.200
Craig Mitchell worked for me
for eight years.


00:15:47.278 --> 00:15:50.736
He passed a full security check
and lie detector test every year.


00:15:50.848 --> 00:15:53.442
Didn't leave so much as a scrap of
paper to explain any of it.


00:15:53.551 --> 00:15:56.520
Eight years!
Five as my personal bodyguard.


00:15:56.621 --> 00:15:58.919
I found this and three other
bloody Christmas presents


00:15:59.023 --> 00:16:00.217
I bought him about the house.


00:16:00.291 --> 00:16:01.781
I don't think he smoked.


00:16:02.393 --> 00:16:03.860
And you had to kill him.


00:16:03.928 --> 00:16:07.125
Couldn't bring him in for questioning so
that we might actually learn something.


00:16:07.231 --> 00:16:10.394
When someone says we got people everywhere,
you expect it to be hyperbole.


00:16:10.468 --> 00:16:13.460
Lots of people say that.
Florists use that expression.


00:16:13.571 --> 00:16:17.405
Doesn't mean that they've got somebody
working for them inside the bloody room.


00:16:17.475 --> 00:16:19.739
What the hell is this organization, Bond?


00:16:19.811 --> 00:16:23.440
How can they be everywhere
and we know nothing about them?


00:16:24.482 --> 00:16:27.451
- I assume we found no trace of White.
- No.


00:16:27.552 --> 00:16:28.814
The agent guarding the door in the garage


00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.785
was dead before you passed him
on the stairs.


00:16:30.888 --> 00:16:32.651
I passed him on the stairs? Christ!


00:16:32.757 --> 00:16:35.624
Mitchell must have killed him when he
went out to check the perimeter.


00:16:35.727 --> 00:16:37.422
You're lucky to be here.


00:16:37.495 --> 00:16:39.053
Do you think White's still alive?


00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.927
- Yes, I do.
- What is it?


00:16:40.999 --> 00:16:42.899
Craig Mitchell, 45 years old.


00:16:42.967 --> 00:16:45.401
No living family.
Gave generously to charity.


00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.233
Tell me you know more than that.


00:16:47.305 --> 00:16:49.899
Our moneymen went through
every bill in Mitchell's wallet and house.


00:16:49.974 --> 00:16:53.000
- How much did he have?
- Less than 100 pounds,


00:16:53.111 --> 00:16:55.079
and about the same in euros and dollars.


00:16:55.146 --> 00:16:56.636
Excuse me. Excuse me, ma'am.


00:16:56.748 --> 00:17:00.013
We've done a complete forensic analysis
of every note and its traceable history.


00:17:00.118 --> 00:17:01.779
Not in the mood.


00:17:03.521 --> 00:17:04.920
After you.


00:17:05.757 --> 00:17:07.691
This particular note from
Mitchell's wallet may be of interest.


00:17:07.792 --> 00:17:08.816
<i>Scanning.</i>


00:17:08.926 --> 00:17:11.918
We introduced tagged bills into
Le Chiffre's money-laundering operation


00:17:11.996 --> 00:17:14.157
by intercepting illegal payoffs.


00:17:14.265 --> 00:17:17.257
We traced money through several of
his bank accounts around the world.


00:17:17.335 --> 00:17:18.597
That's pretty thin.


00:17:18.669 --> 00:17:19.863
At the rate money changes hands,


00:17:19.971 --> 00:17:22.098
you could probably find a tenner
in my wallet with a tag.


00:17:22.173 --> 00:17:24.266
That's true, ma'am.
A single bill could be a coincidence,


00:17:24.342 --> 00:17:26.105
but what about a whole stack?


00:17:26.177 --> 00:17:28.441
These bills,
from the same series as Mitchell's,


00:17:28.513 --> 00:17:31.505
were just scanned at a bank
in Port-au-Prince, Haiti,


00:17:31.616 --> 00:17:34.483
deposited in the account of a Mr. Slate.


00:17:35.019 --> 00:17:36.179
Impress me.


00:17:36.287 --> 00:17:38.346
We have a Mr. Edmund Slate
returning to Port-au-Prince


00:17:38.456 --> 00:17:40.549
from Heathrow this morning.


00:17:40.658 --> 00:17:44.389
His entry documents have him staying
at the Hotel Dessalines.


00:17:44.495 --> 00:17:46.326
He's in room 325.


00:17:55.873 --> 00:17:58.000
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:20:06.204 --> 00:20:08.638
Do you have any messages for 325?


00:20:10.808 --> 00:20:12.969
No, sir.
The only message was about the briefcase


00:20:13.044 --> 00:20:14.534
that was delivered earlier.


00:20:14.645 --> 00:20:17.478
- Did you want us to continue holding it?
- No. No, I'll take that now.


00:20:17.548 --> 00:20:18.845
Yes, sir.


00:20:22.153 --> 00:20:23.848
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:20:32.463 --> 00:20:33.691
Get in!


00:20:34.298 --> 00:20:35.959
- What?
- Get in.


00:20:38.803 --> 00:20:39.997
All right.


00:20:43.574 --> 00:20:44.700
You're late.


00:20:44.809 --> 00:20:46.834
I got pulled into a meeting.


00:20:46.911 --> 00:20:48.344
Who with?


00:20:48.412 --> 00:20:50.505
A friend of Mr. White's.


00:20:51.249 --> 00:20:53.376
Don't think I know him.


00:20:57.188 --> 00:20:58.314
It's funny.


00:20:58.389 --> 00:21:00.357
You don't look at all like I expected.


00:21:00.691 --> 00:21:02.659
Really? What were you expecting?


00:21:02.727 --> 00:21:05.195
I didn't think geologists looked so...


00:21:05.263 --> 00:21:06.423
So?


00:21:09.734 --> 00:21:11.725
A friend of yours?


00:21:11.836 --> 00:21:13.861
I don't have any friends.


00:21:20.878 --> 00:21:23.176
Get out of the way! Move!


00:21:35.059 --> 00:21:36.959
We didn't settle on a price.


00:21:37.061 --> 00:21:38.722
Make me an offer.


00:21:39.797 --> 00:21:42.459
We can work it out later, over drinks.


00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:47.731
Dominic didn't give you any trouble,
did he?


00:21:47.805 --> 00:21:49.067
No.


00:21:53.544 --> 00:21:55.444
What the hell is this?


00:21:55.546 --> 00:21:58.037
I think someone wants to kill you.


00:22:04.221 --> 00:22:06.121
That wasn't very nice.


00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:12.423
- You were supposed to shoot her.
- Well, I missed.


00:22:23.107 --> 00:22:24.472
Get Bond.


00:22:25.776 --> 00:22:29.109
- Where is he now?
- Approaching the docks, Kings Quay.


00:22:32.416 --> 00:22:34.111
<i>- Connecting.
- Tanner.</i>


00:22:34.185 --> 00:22:35.243
I've got Bond.


00:22:35.319 --> 00:22:36.445
Ask him about Slate.


00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:38.147
<i>She wants to know about Slate.</i>


00:22:38.255 --> 00:22:39.813
Tell her Slate was a dead end.


00:22:39.924 --> 00:22:40.982
Slate was a dead end.


00:22:41.092 --> 00:22:42.320
<i>Connection terminated.</i>


00:22:42.426 --> 00:22:44.121
Damn him. He killed him.


00:23:17.228 --> 00:23:19.162
Touch me and I'll break your wrist.


00:23:30.508 --> 00:23:31.805
Camille.


00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:34.675
How nice to see you.


00:23:35.246 --> 00:23:36.873
Alive, you mean?


00:23:38.182 --> 00:23:41.208
I knew we shouldn't have slept together.


00:23:41.318 --> 00:23:43.718
I think I'm starting to like you.


00:23:43.821 --> 00:23:46.585
So you did just try and have me killed.


00:23:47.525 --> 00:23:51.484
And that made me very sad
thinking I would never see you again.


00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.193
But here you are.


00:23:54.265 --> 00:23:57.098
Damn it, Dominic!
I was trying to help you.


00:24:00.604 --> 00:24:03.038
I was trying to uncover a leak.


00:24:03.107 --> 00:24:05.268
And you, you sent someone to kill me?


00:24:05.376 --> 00:24:08.243
Please don't talk to me like I'm stupid!


00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:11.541
It's unattractive.


00:24:13.951 --> 00:24:16.613
Come. I wanna show you something.


00:24:18.722 --> 00:24:19.882
Come.


00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:22.619
There's nothing that makes me
more uncomfortable


00:24:22.726 --> 00:24:25.126
than friends talking behind my back.


00:24:25.229 --> 00:24:26.890
It feels like


00:24:27.731 --> 00:24:29.699
ants under my skin.


00:24:30.634 --> 00:24:33.102
It's been that way forever.


00:24:33.204 --> 00:24:35.229
I remember when I was 15,


00:24:35.873 --> 00:24:39.365
I had a crush on
one of my mother's piano students.


00:24:40.077 --> 00:24:44.741
Somehow I overheard her saying
very nasty things about me.


00:24:45.983 --> 00:24:47.746
I got so angry.


00:24:48.986 --> 00:24:50.715
I took an iron.


00:24:54.124 --> 00:24:55.557
Is that him?


00:24:56.427 --> 00:24:58.895
I... We only spoke on the phone.


00:25:01.499 --> 00:25:05.128
It's such a shame
because he's one of my best geologists.


00:25:05.669 --> 00:25:08.570
He said you asked to buy information.


00:25:09.673 --> 00:25:12.972
No. He called me
and offered to sell me information.


00:25:15.079 --> 00:25:17.980
Why would I come back here
if I was lying?


00:25:18.816 --> 00:25:20.249
Because you love me.


00:25:20.317 --> 00:25:22.444
I was doing it for you.


00:25:22.520 --> 00:25:24.954
To stop him from betraying you.


00:25:26.657 --> 00:25:30.093
You know what burns more
than all your bullshit?


00:25:30.928 --> 00:25:34.364
Is that I always got the feeling
that you were only sleeping with me


00:25:34.465 --> 00:25:36.626
to get to General Medrano.


00:25:38.702 --> 00:25:40.294
Is that him?


00:25:41.138 --> 00:25:44.198
You know how these
deposed dictators are,


00:25:44.308 --> 00:25:46.333
jealous of their safety.


00:25:48.312 --> 00:25:49.870
Stick around.


00:25:50.648 --> 00:25:52.445
I'll introduce you.


00:25:54.485 --> 00:25:56.112
Do you see the girl
that just walked in here?


00:25:56.186 --> 00:25:59.280
Could you give her that?
Tell her to call me.


00:26:17.541 --> 00:26:22.001
<i>You've reached Universal Exports.
Our offices are currently closed.</i>


00:26:29.753 --> 00:26:32.153
And you can do all this for me?


00:26:33.157 --> 00:26:36.149
Well, look at what we
did to this country.


00:26:36.226 --> 00:26:37.659
The Haitians elect a priest


00:26:37.728 --> 00:26:42.358
who decides to raise the minimum wage
from 38 cents to $1 a day.


00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:46.036
It's not a lot,
but it's enough to upset the corporations


00:26:46.103 --> 00:26:49.561
who were here making T-shirts
and running shoes.


00:26:49.673 --> 00:26:53.734
So they called us,
and we facilitated a change.


00:26:53.844 --> 00:26:54.902
The difference is,


00:26:55.012 --> 00:26:59.176
my country's not some flyspeck
in the middle of the Caribbean.


00:26:59.249 --> 00:27:02.685
But we've already begun
destabilizing the government.


00:27:02.753 --> 00:27:05.187
We'll supply the private security.


00:27:05.255 --> 00:27:07.416
We'll pay off the right officials,


00:27:07.524 --> 00:27:11.460
and we have 26 countries
ready to officially recognize


00:27:11.562 --> 00:27:14.030
your new Bolivian government.


00:27:15.032 --> 00:27:17.262
You want your country back.


00:27:17.635 --> 00:27:20.968
My organization can give it to you
within the week.


00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:24.701
You've been busy.


00:27:25.075 --> 00:27:27.543
And in return you want what?


00:27:28.712 --> 00:27:30.111
A desert.


00:27:37.221 --> 00:27:39.781
- This part.
- This land is worthless.


00:27:41.759 --> 00:27:43.784
So you're getting a great deal.


00:27:43.894 --> 00:27:45.828
You won't find oil there.


00:27:45.929 --> 00:27:47.954
Everyone has tried.


00:27:48.065 --> 00:27:50.397
Maybe, maybe not.


00:27:51.335 --> 00:27:54.236
But we own whatever we find.


00:28:01.745 --> 00:28:04.612
Did you know Ernesto Montes?


00:28:04.682 --> 00:28:07.116
A very powerful man in his day.


00:28:07.184 --> 00:28:09.652
He had a beautiful Russian wife.


00:28:10.587 --> 00:28:11.918
A dancer.


00:28:12.756 --> 00:28:15.190
Well, his daughter works for me.


00:28:15.793 --> 00:28:17.090
Or did.


00:28:17.761 --> 00:28:19.251
She's lovely,


00:28:19.797 --> 00:28:21.924
but I don't see the resemblance.


00:28:21.999 --> 00:28:25.799
Why don't you consider her
as something to sweeten the deal?


00:28:28.706 --> 00:28:32.642
Just promise me to drop her
over the side when you're done.


00:28:34.278 --> 00:28:36.940
Camille, General Medrano.


00:28:52.796 --> 00:28:55.560
Be careful what you wish for, my dear.


00:29:04.808 --> 00:29:06.070
Have fun, you two.


00:30:25.255 --> 00:30:26.279
What the hell are you doing?


00:30:26.390 --> 00:30:28.415
- You're welcome!
- You idiot! Take me back!


00:30:28.492 --> 00:30:31.086
You know, maybe I'll do that later.


00:30:34.598 --> 00:30:36.759
You're not one of Greene's.


00:30:37.935 --> 00:30:39.493
Dominic Greene?


00:30:43.073 --> 00:30:44.404
Get down!


00:31:09.266 --> 00:31:11.496
- Give me the wheel!
- Navigate!


00:31:17.608 --> 00:31:18.700
Left!


00:31:29.720 --> 00:31:31.950
- What are you doing?
- Hold on!


00:31:48.805 --> 00:31:50.136
Get down!


00:33:09.920 --> 00:33:11.410
Excuse me.


00:33:11.488 --> 00:33:13.649
Thank you. She's seasick.


00:33:46.256 --> 00:33:47.689
It's Bond.


00:33:47.791 --> 00:33:49.850
<i>- Connect Bond.
- Connecting 007.</i>


00:33:49.960 --> 00:33:50.984
Yes?


00:33:51.094 --> 00:33:53.255
Name check, Dominic Greene.


00:33:53.330 --> 00:33:55.127
<i>G- R-E-E-N-E.</i>


00:33:57.768 --> 00:33:58.792
I might need a little more than that.


00:33:58.869 --> 00:33:59.927
There are a lot of Dominic Greenes.


00:34:00.003 --> 00:34:01.994
Do you have a social security
or passport number?


00:34:02.105 --> 00:34:03.367
No.


00:34:03.473 --> 00:34:04.804
<i>Scanning DGSE databases.</i>


00:34:04.875 --> 00:34:07.844
<i>- Anything?
- Scanning KGB databases.</i>


00:34:07.944 --> 00:34:10.139
Do you have anything?
Will you put her on, please?


00:34:10.213 --> 00:34:12.807
I am on, Bond. What happened to Slate?


00:34:12.883 --> 00:34:14.111
I'm not dwelling on the past.


00:34:14.184 --> 00:34:16.311
- I don't think you should, either.
- You killed him.


00:34:16.386 --> 00:34:19.378
Largest hit, Dominic Greene,
CEO of Greene Planet.


00:34:19.489 --> 00:34:21.354
It's a utility company,


00:34:21.425 --> 00:34:23.893
but Greene's been doing
a lot of philanthropic work,


00:34:23.994 --> 00:34:26.724
buying up large tracts of land
for ecological preserves.


00:34:26.830 --> 00:34:29.822
<i>You should be getting
his picture now.</i>


00:34:29.900 --> 00:34:31.527
Yep, that's him.


00:34:32.069 --> 00:34:34.264
I'm afraid there's a firewall
around his other corporate holdings,


00:34:34.371 --> 00:34:35.565
so we have no other information.


00:34:35.672 --> 00:34:37.105
Get me the Americans.


00:34:37.207 --> 00:34:38.606
<i>Connecting.</i>


00:34:38.708 --> 00:34:39.732
<i>Go ahead.</i>


00:34:39.843 --> 00:34:42.505
Interest in Dominic Greene,
Greene Planet.


00:34:42.579 --> 00:34:44.342
<i>Transferring you now.</i>


00:34:46.249 --> 00:34:48.513
<i>Hold for Gregory Beam, please.</i>


00:34:49.419 --> 00:34:50.443
<i>Thank you.</i>


00:34:50.554 --> 00:34:52.454
<i>Hi, this is Gregory Beam, ma 'am.</i>


00:34:52.556 --> 00:34:54.183
Hello, Mr. Beam.


00:34:54.257 --> 00:34:57.852
I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.
We have no interest in Mr. Greene.


00:34:57.928 --> 00:34:59.361
Thank you, Mr. Beam.


00:34:59.429 --> 00:35:00.521
<i>Connection terminated.</i>


00:35:00.597 --> 00:35:02.360
He's a person of extreme interest.


00:35:02.432 --> 00:35:04.866
- But he just said that he wasn't...
- Tanner, I asked about the man


00:35:04.935 --> 00:35:07.563
and she transferred me
to the section chief of South America.


00:35:07.637 --> 00:35:09.867
How would she know to do that
if they weren't tracking him?


00:35:15.212 --> 00:35:17.646
<i>Bond, we have your location
as approaching an airfield.</i>


00:35:17.747 --> 00:35:19.578
<i>- Is Greene on the move?
- Yeah.</i>


00:35:19.649 --> 00:35:22.880
I've got a tail number,
Golf-Zero-Charlie-Sierra-Charlie.


00:35:22.953 --> 00:35:23.977
<i>Get me a destination.</i>


00:35:27.724 --> 00:35:29.214
It's a private charter


00:35:29.292 --> 00:35:32.386
going to Bregenz, Austria,
leaving immediately.


00:35:32.929 --> 00:35:35.557
Tanner, authorize a charter for 007.


00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.163
And, Bond, if you could avoid killing
every possible lead,


00:35:40.270 --> 00:35:41.464
it would be deeply appreciated.


00:35:42.005 --> 00:35:44.235
Yes, ma'am. I'll do my best.


00:35:44.774 --> 00:35:46.401
<i>Connection terminated.</i>


00:35:46.476 --> 00:35:47.738
I've heard that before.


00:35:50.780 --> 00:35:52.111
- Hello.
- Hi.


00:35:52.582 --> 00:35:54.174
Welcome aboard.


00:35:57.420 --> 00:35:59.183
Come. Have a seat.


00:35:59.923 --> 00:36:02.016
Charlie-Sierra-Charlie.


00:36:17.274 --> 00:36:18.434
Jeez.


00:36:18.942 --> 00:36:20.273
Sorry.


00:36:23.947 --> 00:36:25.812
How much longer?


00:36:27.984 --> 00:36:30.043
So do we have an understanding?


00:36:31.154 --> 00:36:32.178
Yeah.


00:36:32.289 --> 00:36:34.655
We do nothing to stop a coup in Bolivia,
and in exchange,


00:36:34.724 --> 00:36:39.218
the new government gives America
the lease to any oil found.


00:36:40.664 --> 00:36:42.655
If it's oil you want.


00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:46.567
Well, you didn't find diamonds, did you?


00:36:52.075 --> 00:36:55.636
Drilling underground, you kept off
everybody's radar for a very long time,


00:36:55.712 --> 00:36:59.876
but you can't buy that much piping
without somebody getting curious.


00:37:00.984 --> 00:37:02.975
We'll have to verify the find.


00:37:03.053 --> 00:37:07.490
I'm not even admitting there is one.
You are getting this for free.


00:37:08.491 --> 00:37:11.324
Venezuela, Brazil, now Bolivia.


00:37:11.394 --> 00:37:16.058
With you tied up in the Middle East,
South America is falling like dominoes.


00:37:17.500 --> 00:37:22.335
You don't need another Marxist giving
national resources to the people, do you?


00:37:23.006 --> 00:37:25.031
Well, we can hardly be expected
to do something about a coup


00:37:25.108 --> 00:37:27.042
we know nothing about.


00:37:30.513 --> 00:37:32.674
And I have a pest.


00:37:34.351 --> 00:37:35.511
This.


00:37:38.722 --> 00:37:41.190
You have any idea who that is?


00:37:51.268 --> 00:37:52.599
Sorry.


00:37:55.038 --> 00:37:57.768
It's James Bond, British Secret Service.


00:37:58.742 --> 00:38:01.643
I don't know how I
could have missed that.


00:38:03.213 --> 00:38:05.977
I will need you to get rid of him for me.


00:38:06.082 --> 00:38:08.710
Yeah. That's not gonna be a problem.


00:38:25.502 --> 00:38:27.663
You know who Greene is
and you wanna put us in bed with him.


00:38:27.771 --> 00:38:29.739
You are kidding, right?


00:38:29.806 --> 00:38:33.139
Yeah. You're right.
We should just deal with nice people.


00:38:33.243 --> 00:38:35.939
I need to know you're on the team, Felix.


00:38:36.012 --> 00:38:38.606
I need to know you value your career.


00:39:51.221 --> 00:39:52.848
Dominic Greene.


00:40:11.574 --> 00:40:13.371
- Good to see you. Good.
- How are you?


00:40:13.443 --> 00:40:14.876
Thank you.


00:40:49.779 --> 00:40:51.804
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>


00:40:51.915 --> 00:40:55.373
<i>tonight's performance of Tosca
will begin shortly.</i>


00:40:55.452 --> 00:40:57.443
<i>Please take your seats.</i>


00:41:52.041 --> 00:41:54.805
<i>What else does General
Medrano require?</i>


00:42:16.966 --> 00:42:19.400
<i>Anything further
from Canadian intelligence?</i>


00:42:19.502 --> 00:42:21.561
<i>We'll discuss that later.</i>


00:42:22.071 --> 00:42:24.437
<i>How much more pipeline do we need?</i>


00:42:24.541 --> 00:42:27.066
Ideally, 2,000 kilometers.


00:42:27.544 --> 00:42:29.603
<i>Are there any objections?</i>


00:42:30.747 --> 00:42:31.771
<i>No.</i>


00:42:31.881 --> 00:42:33.212
<i>Not here.</i>


00:42:33.283 --> 00:42:34.682
<i>No objections.</i>


00:42:35.351 --> 00:42:38.514
Transfer the funds
from our Siberian holdings.


00:42:38.588 --> 00:42:39.885
<i>Done.</i>


00:42:43.426 --> 00:42:45.417
Where do the Americans stand?


00:42:45.528 --> 00:42:49.897
Well, the CIA doesn't care about another
dictator as long as they get their end.


00:42:49.966 --> 00:42:52.526
But when they find out
that they've been duped?


00:42:52.602 --> 00:42:54.570
I'm working on that.


00:42:54.637 --> 00:42:58.266
<i>I'm still not sure that the Tierra Project
is the best use of Quantum 's time.</i>


00:42:58.374 --> 00:43:00.740
<i>Perhaps we should shift
our focus to the Canadian.</i>


00:43:00.810 --> 00:43:03.540
<i>This is the world's
most precious resource.</i>


00:43:03.613 --> 00:43:06.878
<i>We need to control as much
of it as we can.</i>


00:43:06.950 --> 00:43:09.214
Bolivia must be top priority.


00:43:09.285 --> 00:43:11.219
Can I offer an opinion?


00:43:13.556 --> 00:43:17.458
I really think you people
should find a better place to meet.


00:43:23.099 --> 00:43:25.659
Where do you think you're going?


00:43:46.322 --> 00:43:47.914
Thank you.


00:43:57.834 --> 00:44:00.268
<i>Well, Tosca isn't for everyone.</i>


00:45:14.243 --> 00:45:15.676
Drop it.


00:45:19.215 --> 00:45:21.513
So who are you working for?


00:45:21.584 --> 00:45:22.846
Piss off.


00:45:23.186 --> 00:45:27.213
Get rid of anything we brought with us.
We've been compromised.


00:45:30.226 --> 00:45:32.922
I asked you who you were working for.


00:45:44.874 --> 00:45:47.274
- Is he one of ours?
- No.


00:45:47.376 --> 00:45:49.936
Then he shouldn't be looking at me.


00:45:58.588 --> 00:46:00.078
Get me M.


00:46:01.557 --> 00:46:02.888
It's your line.


00:46:02.959 --> 00:46:05.393
Thanks. Connect call.


00:46:05.461 --> 00:46:06.928
<i>Connecting Tanner.</i>


00:46:06.996 --> 00:46:08.463
<i>We've ID'd the pictures.</i>


00:46:08.564 --> 00:46:09.826
Show me.


00:46:09.932 --> 00:46:14.596
Gregor Karakov, former minister,
now owns most of the mines in Siberia,


00:46:14.670 --> 00:46:18.333
<i>Moishe Soref, former Mossad,
now telecom giant,</i>


00:46:18.441 --> 00:46:21.239
<i>and Guy Haines, special envoy
to the Prime Minister.</i>


00:46:21.310 --> 00:46:22.572
Get Bond.


00:46:22.645 --> 00:46:24.408
There's something else.


00:46:24.480 --> 00:46:28.576
<i>It appears Bond shot Haines'
bodyguard and threw him off a roof.</i>


00:46:32.622 --> 00:46:34.419
<i>- Where are you?
- Did you get my pictures?</i>


00:46:34.490 --> 00:46:36.788
Was this a conversation?
Can you link these people?


00:46:36.859 --> 00:46:38.258
<i>Is that stress in your voice?</i>


00:46:38.327 --> 00:46:39.851
I need you to come in and debrief.


00:46:39.962 --> 00:46:43.125
<i>- I don't have time.
- Bond, you killed a man in Bregenz.</i>


00:46:43.199 --> 00:46:44.427
I did my best not to.


00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:46.365
<i>You shot him at point blank
and threw him off a roof.</i>


00:46:46.469 --> 00:46:48.437
I'd hardly call that showing restraint,


00:46:48.504 --> 00:46:50.335
especially since he was
a member of Special Branch.


00:46:54.477 --> 00:46:55.637
So who was he guarding?


00:46:55.711 --> 00:46:56.769
Bond, are you missing the fact


00:46:56.846 --> 00:46:58.336
that you killed a member
of Special Branch?


00:46:58.447 --> 00:47:00.381
I need you to come in.


00:47:00.483 --> 00:47:04.613
And I would, but right now I need to find
the man who tried to kill you.


00:47:04.687 --> 00:47:05.847
<i>Go back to sleep.</i>


00:47:05.955 --> 00:47:07.217
<i>Connection terminated.</i>


00:47:07.323 --> 00:47:08.722
Restrict Bond's movements.


00:47:08.825 --> 00:47:10.452
Cancel his cards.


00:47:10.526 --> 00:47:12.289
Put an alert on his passports.
All of them.


00:47:12.361 --> 00:47:14.625
And I want to know everything
we don't know about Haines.


00:47:14.697 --> 00:47:15.721
<i>Yes, ma 'am.</i>


00:47:15.832 --> 00:47:18.960
And, Tanner,
be careful who you trust with this.


00:47:19.035 --> 00:47:21.401
Hopefully, you're a better judge
of character than I am.


00:47:23.005 --> 00:47:25.473
You want to follow your friends
to La Paz, Bolivia?


00:47:25.541 --> 00:47:26.803
Please.


00:47:29.212 --> 00:47:30.804
I'm sorry, sir, but this doesn't work.


00:47:30.880 --> 00:47:33.212
Do you have another card?


00:47:33.316 --> 00:47:34.476
No.


00:47:39.889 --> 00:47:41.880
Could you do me a favor?


00:47:41.991 --> 00:47:43.822
You're gonna get a
phone call in a minute.


00:47:43.893 --> 00:47:47.329
Would you mind telling them
I'm headed for Cairo?


00:47:47.396 --> 00:47:49.762
- I'd be happy to.
- Thank you.


00:48:29.772 --> 00:48:31.103
Mathis.


00:48:31.908 --> 00:48:33.773
What do you want?


00:48:33.876 --> 00:48:35.537
Come to apologize?


00:48:37.947 --> 00:48:39.710
You know, Mathis,


00:48:40.249 --> 00:48:42.479
I think retirement suits you.


00:48:43.252 --> 00:48:44.776
None for him.


00:48:45.388 --> 00:48:47.652
Sorry. He's in a bad mood today.


00:49:11.180 --> 00:49:13.410
I need a passport
and matching credit cards.


00:49:14.317 --> 00:49:16.512
And Ml6 ran out of plastic?


00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:20.582
Well, oddly, right now,
you're the only person I think I can trust.


00:49:20.656 --> 00:49:22.351
That is odd.


00:49:22.458 --> 00:49:24.289
But I guess when one's young,


00:49:24.360 --> 00:49:28.091
it seems very easy to distinguish
between right and wrong.


00:49:28.164 --> 00:49:31.133
But as one gets older,
it becomes more difficult.


00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:34.192
The villains and the heroes
get all mixed up.


00:49:35.171 --> 00:49:37.605
I was sorry to hear about Vesper.


00:49:38.107 --> 00:49:39.972
I think she loved you.


00:49:41.110 --> 00:49:43.442
Right up until the moment
she betrayed me.


00:49:44.347 --> 00:49:46.008
She died for you.


00:49:48.117 --> 00:49:50.483
Why did you really want to see me?


00:49:52.121 --> 00:49:54.055
I need some information.


00:49:58.194 --> 00:50:02.460
You have some hard friends.
This man is some kind of facilitator.


00:50:02.531 --> 00:50:05.898
Fingers in many pies,
and they don't leave any prints.


00:50:06.002 --> 00:50:09.631
- These men were together?
- They're buying up oil pipeline.


00:50:09.705 --> 00:50:11.195
Something called the Tierra Project.


00:50:11.307 --> 00:50:13.673
- Do you know it?
- Destroy these.


00:50:13.743 --> 00:50:16.143
That's Guy Haines. You don't know him?


00:50:16.212 --> 00:50:18.146
- Should I?
- I suppose not.


00:50:18.214 --> 00:50:21.274
You haven't been keeping
secrets as long as I have.


00:50:21.384 --> 00:50:23.352
He keeps a very low profile,


00:50:23.419 --> 00:50:27.082
but he's one of the Prime Minister's
closest advisors.


00:50:27.189 --> 00:50:30.750
Well, they say you're judged
by the strength of your enemies.


00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:32.953
Do you know anything about Bolivia?


00:50:33.062 --> 00:50:36.259
I was stationed in South America
for seven years.


00:50:36.365 --> 00:50:39.198
- Well, do you have some contacts there?
- A few.


00:50:39.635 --> 00:50:41.762
What do you want to know?


00:50:42.638 --> 00:50:44.105
Come with me.


00:51:14.837 --> 00:51:16.600
You can't sleep?


00:51:17.173 --> 00:51:19.004
May I fix you a drink, sir?


00:51:19.108 --> 00:51:21.008
What are you drinking?


00:51:21.777 --> 00:51:23.802
I don't know. What am I drinking?


00:51:23.913 --> 00:51:27.349
Three measures of Gordon's gin,
one of vodka, half of...


00:51:27.450 --> 00:51:30.476
- Kina Lillet.
- Kina Lillet, which is not Vermouth,


00:51:30.586 --> 00:51:32.281
shaken well until it is ice-cold,


00:51:32.354 --> 00:51:35.653
then served
with a large thin slice of lemon peel.


00:51:36.192 --> 00:51:37.682
Six of them.


00:51:38.027 --> 00:51:39.688
That's impressive.


00:51:39.795 --> 00:51:42.195
They're good. You should have one.


00:51:42.298 --> 00:51:44.789
No, it'll just keep me awake.


00:51:49.205 --> 00:51:51.537
So what's keeping you awake?


00:51:54.276 --> 00:51:56.938
I was wondering why you came with me.


00:51:58.547 --> 00:52:01.778
It takes something
to admit you were wrong.


00:52:04.787 --> 00:52:07.153
- You want a sleeping pill?
- No.


00:52:07.223 --> 00:52:08.850
- Pain pill?
- No.


00:52:08.958 --> 00:52:11.051
I have pills for everything.


00:52:11.560 --> 00:52:13.528
Some make you taller.


00:52:14.630 --> 00:52:16.495
Some make you forget.


00:52:19.802 --> 00:52:22.236
I'm going to try and get some sleep.


00:52:22.338 --> 00:52:23.669
Good idea.


00:52:38.654 --> 00:52:40.053
Thank you.


00:52:40.523 --> 00:52:43.515
Mr. Bond, my name is Fields.
I'm from the consulate.


00:52:43.592 --> 00:52:44.650
Well, of course you are.


00:52:44.727 --> 00:52:46.024
And what do you do
at the consulate, Fields?


00:52:46.095 --> 00:52:47.392
That's not important.


00:52:47.496 --> 00:52:48.724
My orders are to turn you around


00:52:48.831 --> 00:52:50.856
and put you on the first plane
back to London.


00:52:50.933 --> 00:52:53.697
Do those orders include my friend Mathis?


00:52:53.769 --> 00:52:55.498
I'm sorry, I don't know who you are.


00:52:55.571 --> 00:52:58.734
You see that? Gone such a short time
and already forgotten.


00:52:58.841 --> 00:53:00.502
You're just saying that to hurt me.


00:53:00.609 --> 00:53:03.737
Mr. Bond, these orders come from
the highest possible authority.


00:53:03.846 --> 00:53:06.781
Taxi.
Fields, when is the next flight to London?


00:53:06.882 --> 00:53:08.281
Tomorrow morning.


00:53:08.384 --> 00:53:09.408
Well then, we have all night.


00:53:09.518 --> 00:53:11.042
If you attempt to flee,
I will arrest you,


00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:13.588
drop you off in jail
and take you to the plane in chains.


00:53:13.689 --> 00:53:16.180
- Understand?
- Perfectly. After you.


00:53:18.194 --> 00:53:21.027
- I think she has handcuffs.
- I do hope so.


00:53:29.805 --> 00:53:31.636
He blames the water shortage
on global warming.


00:53:32.942 --> 00:53:34.034
Hello, Carlos? Carlos.


00:53:38.814 --> 00:53:40.372
The Colonel who heads
the National Police.


00:54:05.741 --> 00:54:07.732
We have a reservation.


00:54:08.577 --> 00:54:10.067
<i>- Cómo está?
- Very well, thank you.</i>


00:54:10.145 --> 00:54:12.511
- Your name?
- Miss Fields.


00:54:17.253 --> 00:54:19.153
- You're going nowhere.
- So shoot me.


00:54:19.255 --> 00:54:20.279
I'd rather stay in a morgue.


00:54:20.356 --> 00:54:23.587
We are teachers on sabbatical.
This fits our cover.


00:54:23.659 --> 00:54:26.423
No, it doesn't. Get in. Get in!


00:54:52.821 --> 00:54:54.482
Follow me, please.


00:55:02.131 --> 00:55:04.691
<i>- May I show you your room, señor?
- No, it's fine. Thank you.</i>


00:55:22.651 --> 00:55:24.812
I can't find the...


00:55:25.587 --> 00:55:27.214
The stationery.


00:55:28.090 --> 00:55:30.285
Will you come and help me look?


00:55:44.540 --> 00:55:46.735
You've been invited to a party.


00:55:46.842 --> 00:55:49.436
I didn't know we had any friends here.


00:55:50.512 --> 00:55:52.002
Greene Planet.


00:55:53.215 --> 00:55:54.239
You're not coming?


00:55:54.350 --> 00:55:56.511
I'm having a drink
with my friend the Colonel.


00:55:56.585 --> 00:55:58.917
I'll see you there later.


00:56:03.859 --> 00:56:06.555
Do you know how angry I am at myself?


00:56:07.062 --> 00:56:08.859
I can't imagine.


00:56:11.567 --> 00:56:13.467
You must be furious.


00:56:20.042 --> 00:56:22.272
Do you want to go to a party?


00:56:22.911 --> 00:56:24.139
A party?


00:56:24.980 --> 00:56:27.107
But I have nothing to wear.


00:56:27.549 --> 00:56:28.573
We'll fix that.


00:56:48.237 --> 00:56:50.569
It might be useful to
know your real name.


00:56:50.639 --> 00:56:52.072
Fields.


00:56:54.676 --> 00:56:56.166
Just Fields.


00:56:57.179 --> 00:56:58.806
Fields it is, then.


00:56:58.914 --> 00:57:02.680
<i>We are in a spiral
of environmental decline.</i>


00:57:03.786 --> 00:57:09.918
<i>Since 1945, 17% of the
planet's vegetated surface</i>


00:57:09.992 --> 00:57:12.859
<i>has been irreversibly degraded.</i>


00:57:13.629 --> 00:57:19.033
<i>The Tierra Project is just one small part
of a global network of Eco Parks</i>


00:57:19.134 --> 00:57:21.159
<i>that Greene Planet has created</i>


00:57:21.270 --> 00:57:25.673
<i>to rejuvenate a world
on the verge of collapse.</i>


00:57:27.443 --> 00:57:31.607
<i>I hope that tonight you make
the decision to be part of that.</i>


00:57:33.649 --> 00:57:34.980
<i>Thank you.</i>


00:57:39.288 --> 00:57:40.778
<i>And have fun.</i>


00:57:41.323 --> 00:57:43.518
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.


00:57:44.293 --> 00:57:46.318
Excellent speech and congratulations.


00:57:46.395 --> 00:57:48.522
Wonderful speech, Dominic.


00:57:48.630 --> 00:57:50.530
- We need you here.
- Thank you.


00:57:50.632 --> 00:57:53.897
Miss Fields, Mr. Bond, my friend Carlos.


00:57:54.002 --> 00:57:55.833
- Pleased to meet you.
- Ma'am.


00:57:56.905 --> 00:57:59.897
Mr. Bond, Mathis has spoken
a great deal about you.


00:58:00.008 --> 00:58:03.876
I want you to know my entire
police force is at your disposal.


00:58:04.246 --> 00:58:05.679
Well, that could be very useful.


00:58:05.747 --> 00:58:09.012
You know, there are people in this
country spending half their paycheck


00:58:09.084 --> 00:58:10.574
just to get clean water.


00:58:10.686 --> 00:58:11.710
What do you think of that?


00:58:11.820 --> 00:58:13.879
The Bolivian government is the problem.


00:58:13.989 --> 00:58:15.581
They cut down the trees,


00:58:15.691 --> 00:58:19.855
then act surprised when the water
and the soil wash out to sea.


00:58:19.928 --> 00:58:23.420
I couldn't agree more.
I hope this figure is to your liking.


00:58:23.532 --> 00:58:25.898
<i>Chéri, you shouldn't tease.</i>


00:58:26.001 --> 00:58:30.028
Why don't you tell them about all
the land you bought up outside Potosí?


00:58:30.105 --> 00:58:32.335
It's been a pleasure. Will you excuse me?


00:58:32.407 --> 00:58:33.738
Of course.


00:58:33.842 --> 00:58:34.934
Somehow the logging rights


00:58:35.043 --> 00:58:39.173
went to a multinational corporation
that cut down the forests,


00:58:39.248 --> 00:58:43.947
but only after our last government
sold the land to Greene Planet.


00:58:45.888 --> 00:58:49.289
- Or have I got my facts crossed?
- Yes, I think you did.


00:58:50.058 --> 00:58:51.958
You'll excuse us?


00:58:52.728 --> 00:58:54.696
What a wonderful night.


00:58:57.966 --> 00:59:00.594
You just cost me
quite a bit of money, darling.


00:59:00.702 --> 00:59:03.364
You can't put a price on integrity.


00:59:03.472 --> 00:59:04.803
I can try.


00:59:10.546 --> 00:59:11.877
Thank you.


00:59:11.947 --> 00:59:15.906
Tell me you didn't drop by tonight
just to piss on my parade.


00:59:16.018 --> 00:59:19.920
Or are you still after
this General's head for your mantel?


00:59:20.022 --> 00:59:21.512
A little of both.


00:59:21.590 --> 00:59:23.080
Tell me where Medrano is


00:59:23.191 --> 00:59:26.251
and maybe you won't lose
any more investors.


00:59:29.865 --> 00:59:34.234
You are really breaking my heart,
choosing an insect like that over me.


00:59:35.771 --> 00:59:37.534
Are you going to throw me over?


00:59:37.606 --> 00:59:40.871
No. You've been drinking,
so maybe you slipped.


00:59:41.710 --> 00:59:44.201
Just think how much you'd miss me.


00:59:49.651 --> 00:59:51.141
Good evening.


00:59:51.253 --> 00:59:52.777
There you are.


00:59:54.656 --> 00:59:56.624
Would you excuse me?


00:59:56.725 --> 00:59:58.056
Mr. Bond.


00:59:59.061 --> 01:00:00.722
What a pleasure.


01:00:02.898 --> 01:00:05.059
Well, careful with this one.
She won't go to bed with you


01:00:05.133 --> 01:00:07.829
unless you give her something
she really wants.


01:00:07.936 --> 01:00:10.063
It's a shame
because she's really quite stunning


01:00:10.138 --> 01:00:12.971
once you get her on her back.


01:00:13.075 --> 01:00:15.737
I wish I could say
the feeling was mutual.


01:00:15.811 --> 01:00:17.108
I'm sorry, Mr. Greene, but we have to go.


01:00:17.179 --> 01:00:19.477
Please. My friends call me Dominic.


01:00:19.581 --> 01:00:21.242
I'm sure they do.


01:00:22.250 --> 01:00:24.741
How much do you know
about Bond, Camille?


01:00:24.820 --> 01:00:27.084
Because he's rather a tragic case.


01:00:27.155 --> 01:00:30.090
As Ml6 says, he's difficult to control.


01:00:30.158 --> 01:00:34.822
Nice way of saying that everything
he touches seems to wither and die.


01:00:34.930 --> 01:00:36.124
Shall we?


01:00:36.198 --> 01:00:38.758
Doesn't bode well for you, I'm afraid.


01:00:38.834 --> 01:00:40.927
You two do make
a charming couple, though.


01:00:41.003 --> 01:00:43.938
You're both... What's the expression?


01:00:44.006 --> 01:00:45.598
Damaged goods.


01:00:49.044 --> 01:00:50.511
Oh, my gosh!


01:00:51.480 --> 01:00:53.004
I'm so sorry.


01:00:56.785 --> 01:00:57.945
Come on, lighten up.


01:00:58.020 --> 01:01:00.011
You're cramping my style.


01:01:00.989 --> 01:01:02.957
So it's British intelligence now.


01:01:03.025 --> 01:01:04.617
What the hell do you want from me?


01:01:04.693 --> 01:01:07.457
You're gonna show me
Dominic Greene's Tierra Project.


01:01:07.529 --> 01:01:09.554
- Are you up to it?
- Do I have a choice?


01:01:09.665 --> 01:01:11.462
Do you want one?


01:01:11.533 --> 01:01:14.400
There's something horribly
efficient about you.


01:01:14.503 --> 01:01:16.300
Is that a compliment?


01:01:29.651 --> 01:01:34.020
Well, what's the bet that Dominic Greene
has friends in the police force?


01:01:45.167 --> 01:01:46.691
Stay here.


01:02:07.589 --> 01:02:10.217
Now, why would you want me to do that?


01:02:41.723 --> 01:02:43.054
Mathis?


01:02:44.926 --> 01:02:47.986
There's a hospital
on the other side of town.


01:02:48.096 --> 01:02:49.427
Please.


01:02:50.465 --> 01:02:52.228
Stay with me.


01:02:52.801 --> 01:02:54.564
Stay here, please.


01:02:55.437 --> 01:02:56.734
Please.


01:02:57.105 --> 01:02:58.504
Come here.


01:03:01.910 --> 01:03:03.309
It's okay.


01:03:05.247 --> 01:03:06.771
That's better.


01:03:07.082 --> 01:03:08.845
That doesn't hurt.


01:03:11.953 --> 01:03:14.080
Is Mathis your cover name?


01:03:15.123 --> 01:03:16.317
Yes.


01:03:18.460 --> 01:03:20.587
Not a very good one, is it?


01:03:26.268 --> 01:03:28.463
Do we forgive each other?


01:03:30.806 --> 01:03:33.274
I shouldn't have left you alone.


01:03:34.843 --> 01:03:36.174
Vesper.


01:03:37.445 --> 01:03:39.606
She gave everything for you.


01:03:41.950 --> 01:03:43.349
Forgive her.


01:03:45.487 --> 01:03:47.284
Forgive yourself.


01:04:08.643 --> 01:04:11.134
Is that how you treat your friends?


01:04:12.581 --> 01:04:14.242
He wouldn't care.


01:04:20.488 --> 01:04:21.853
Let's go.


01:04:36.104 --> 01:04:39.073
<i>The Foreign Secretary's
asking to see you.</i>


01:04:39.674 --> 01:04:41.039
What don't I know?


01:04:41.109 --> 01:04:44.101
<i>René Mathis has been
shot dead in Bolivia.</i>


01:04:44.613 --> 01:04:46.945
<i>The police claim it was Bond.</i>


01:05:21.249 --> 01:05:22.511
<i>How much did you pay him?</i>


01:05:22.584 --> 01:05:25.917
<i>Well, he wanted you,
but I left him the car as collateral.</i>


01:05:26.021 --> 01:05:28.922
<i>He'll make much more
when he sells us out.</i>


01:05:31.626 --> 01:05:32.854
<i>Right.</i>


01:05:33.194 --> 01:05:35.719
<i>Let's see if this thing'll fly.</i>


01:05:50.779 --> 01:05:51.939
<i>Here.</i>


01:05:52.047 --> 01:05:55.539
<i>All the information I found said
there was nothing of value there,</i>


01:05:55.617 --> 01:05:58.780
<i>but Greene's geologist
had proof that there was.</i>


01:06:02.157 --> 01:06:05.593
<i>My sources tell me
you're Bolivian Secret Service,</i>


01:06:06.628 --> 01:06:08.289
<i>or used to be,</i>


01:06:09.230 --> 01:06:12.631
<i>and that you infiltrated Greene's
organization by having sex with him.</i>


01:06:13.568 --> 01:06:16.560
<i>- That offends you?
- No, not in the slightest.</i>


01:06:16.972 --> 01:06:19.236
<i>So what's your interest in Greene?</i>


01:06:19.307 --> 01:06:22.333
<i>Amongst other things,
he tried to kill a friend of mine.</i>


01:06:22.444 --> 01:06:23.911
<i>- A woman?
- Yes.</i>


01:06:24.346 --> 01:06:25.904
<i>But it's not what you think.</i>


01:06:25.981 --> 01:06:28.814
<i>- Your mother?
- She likes to think so.</i>


01:06:32.654 --> 01:06:34.679
<i>What's that down there?</i>


01:06:37.192 --> 01:06:38.921
<i>That's a sinkhole.</i>


01:06:38.994 --> 01:06:41.189
<i>There are a few around here.</i>


01:06:42.263 --> 01:06:45.528
<i>Just for the record,
I wasn't with Greene for my...</i>


01:07:20.702 --> 01:07:21.999
Damn it!


01:07:51.399 --> 01:07:53.230
I think we lost him!


01:08:02.610 --> 01:08:04.339
He's coming fast!


01:08:51.292 --> 01:08:53.317
He's right behind you!


01:09:35.170 --> 01:09:37.161
Here. Put that on!


01:10:22.150 --> 01:10:23.481
Come on!


01:10:44.606 --> 01:10:45.903
Camille!


01:11:05.193 --> 01:11:07.593
According to the Bolivians,
it was a routine stop,


01:11:07.695 --> 01:11:10.493
and when they discovered Mathis' body,
Bond disarmed and shot them.


01:11:10.732 --> 01:11:12.859
Of course, there are no witnesses
to prove otherwise.


01:11:12.934 --> 01:11:15.732
I need something.
I can't go in there unarmed.


01:11:15.837 --> 01:11:17.930
I'm sorry. There's nothing.


01:11:20.341 --> 01:11:21.706
Come in.


01:11:23.111 --> 01:11:26.569
What's today's excuse?
That Bond is legally blind?


01:11:26.681 --> 01:11:27.841
No, Minister.


01:11:27.915 --> 01:11:30.713
I don't think I need to tell you
how upset the PM is.


01:11:31.052 --> 01:11:33.680
With respect, the PM has my direct line.


01:11:33.755 --> 01:11:37.282
And he'd have used it
if he'd wanted to speak to you.


01:11:37.392 --> 01:11:39.860
I'm sorry, M. Things have changed.


01:11:40.461 --> 01:11:43.123
We've had long discussions
with our cousins.


01:11:43.231 --> 01:11:45.426
Mr. Greene's interests
and ours now align.


01:11:45.533 --> 01:11:49.970
Minister, this man is a major player in one
of the most dangerous organizations...


01:11:50.071 --> 01:11:51.936
We've never even heard of.


01:11:52.040 --> 01:11:55.373
Foreign policy cannot be conducted on
the basis of hunches and innuendo.


01:11:55.443 --> 01:11:57.638
Then give us time
to gather enough evidence


01:11:57.745 --> 01:11:59.713
so you can make informed decisions.


01:11:59.781 --> 01:12:01.078
Fine.


01:12:02.283 --> 01:12:05.309
Say you're right.
Say Greene is a villain.


01:12:05.420 --> 01:12:09.914
If we refused to do business with villains,
we'd have almost no one to trade with.


01:12:09.991 --> 01:12:13.154
The world's running out of oil, M.
The Russians aren't playing ball.


01:12:13.261 --> 01:12:15.559
The Americans and Chinese
are dividing up what's left.


01:12:15.630 --> 01:12:18.098
Right or wrong doesn't come into it.


01:12:18.166 --> 01:12:20.566
We're acting out of necessity.


01:12:23.471 --> 01:12:25.803
Bond is running wild.


01:12:27.108 --> 01:12:29.770
Who's to say he hasn't been turned?


01:12:29.844 --> 01:12:33.746
Pull him in
or the Americans will put him down.


01:12:36.918 --> 01:12:39.011
I think I found a way out.


01:12:40.188 --> 01:12:41.917
You're freezing.


01:12:42.757 --> 01:12:43.985
I'm fine.


01:13:00.608 --> 01:13:03.543
So what is it that Greene has
that you want?


01:13:08.649 --> 01:13:12.176
It's not Greene.
It's Medrano, the man he met in Haiti.


01:13:14.389 --> 01:13:17.222
My father worked for the military junta.


01:13:17.825 --> 01:13:19.816
He was a very cruel man,


01:13:21.629 --> 01:13:23.529
but he was my father.


01:13:27.235 --> 01:13:29.294
When I was a small child


01:13:29.370 --> 01:13:32.533
<i>the opposition sent general
Medrano to our house.</i>


01:13:34.842 --> 01:13:36.707
He shot my father.


01:13:37.578 --> 01:13:40.411
He did things to my mother and my sister


01:13:41.382 --> 01:13:44.249
and then strangled them while I watched.


01:13:46.254 --> 01:13:48.882
I was too young to be any trouble,


01:13:50.224 --> 01:13:52.317
so he just smiled at me


01:13:54.762 --> 01:13:56.923
and set the house on fire.


01:13:59.667 --> 01:14:01.328
He left his mark.


01:14:05.239 --> 01:14:06.866
So when I pulled you off the boat...


01:14:06.941 --> 01:14:09.341
I waited years for that chance.


01:14:10.578 --> 01:14:12.170
I apologize.


01:14:14.682 --> 01:14:18.015
It seems we're both using Greene
to get to somebody.


01:14:19.053 --> 01:14:20.850
You lost somebody?


01:14:21.389 --> 01:14:22.754
I did, yes.


01:14:23.758 --> 01:14:25.783
You catch whoever did it?


01:14:26.294 --> 01:14:28.194
No. Not yet.


01:14:29.797 --> 01:14:31.560
Tell me when you do.


01:14:32.433 --> 01:14:34.799
I'd like to know how it feels.


01:14:39.974 --> 01:14:41.566
We should go.


01:14:42.143 --> 01:14:43.405
You ready?


01:15:17.445 --> 01:15:19.504
They used dynamite.


01:15:22.416 --> 01:15:24.748
This used to be a riverbed.


01:15:41.602 --> 01:15:44.867
Greene isn't after the oil.
He wants the water.


01:15:46.173 --> 01:15:47.765
We can't leave it like this.


01:15:47.842 --> 01:15:51.869
It's one dam. He's creating a drought.
He'll have built others.


01:17:22.003 --> 01:17:24.267
Excuse me, sir. Your wife left a message.


01:17:24.372 --> 01:17:27.398
The English woman,
she left it for you this morning.


01:17:27.508 --> 01:17:28.873
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.


01:17:31.445 --> 01:17:32.776
What is it?


01:17:34.081 --> 01:17:36.549
Would you mind waiting down here?


01:17:37.218 --> 01:17:39.049
I'll be outside.


01:17:57.872 --> 01:17:59.897
So that's what she meant.


01:18:00.307 --> 01:18:01.740
I hope you can trust these men.


01:18:01.809 --> 01:18:04.243
Just a moment. It's Tanner.


01:18:05.212 --> 01:18:06.406
Yes?


01:18:07.481 --> 01:18:08.880
We've got the girl downstairs.


01:18:08.949 --> 01:18:11.144
She says to tell you she's sorry
but this is not her fight.


01:18:11.252 --> 01:18:12.879
It isn't. Let her go.


01:18:12.953 --> 01:18:14.887
She isn't our concern.


01:18:15.489 --> 01:18:17.218
Well, I'm disappointed.


01:18:17.758 --> 01:18:18.782
You are?


01:18:18.893 --> 01:18:20.986
How much oil
did the Americans promise you?


01:18:21.095 --> 01:18:22.153
This isn't about oil.


01:18:22.263 --> 01:18:25.426
- Well, that's good, because there isn't any.
- It's about trust.


01:18:25.499 --> 01:18:27.330
You said you weren't motivated
by revenge.


01:18:27.435 --> 01:18:29.926
- I'm motivated by my duty.
- No.


01:18:30.938 --> 01:18:33.930
I think you are so blinded
by inconsolable rage


01:18:34.008 --> 01:18:36.408
that you don't care who you hurt.


01:18:36.477 --> 01:18:40.675
When you can't tell your friends
from your enemies, it's time to go.


01:18:47.621 --> 01:18:50.988
You might like to tell her your theory
about there being no oil.


01:18:51.092 --> 01:18:53.185
Her lungs are full of it.


01:18:54.595 --> 01:18:57.120
- It was Greene.
- No doubt. But why?


01:18:58.632 --> 01:19:01.795
- It's just misdirection.
- I mean, why her, Bond?


01:19:01.869 --> 01:19:06.932
She was just supposed to send you home.
She worked in an office, collecting reports.


01:19:07.441 --> 01:19:10.137
Look how well your charm works, James.


01:19:10.444 --> 01:19:13.277
They'll do anything for you, won't they?


01:19:13.514 --> 01:19:15.482
How many is that now?


01:19:16.050 --> 01:19:19.952
You're removed from duty and suspended
pending further investigation.


01:19:20.020 --> 01:19:24.650
You'll give whatever weapons you have
to these men and leave with them now.


01:20:09.603 --> 01:20:11.594
Miss Fields showed true bravery.


01:20:11.705 --> 01:20:13.605
I want that mentioned in your report.


01:20:13.707 --> 01:20:16.676
- Now you and I need to see this through.
- There's nowhere to go.


01:20:16.744 --> 01:20:19.713
There's a capture or
kill order out on you.


01:20:20.414 --> 01:20:22.507
Who would have done that?


01:20:31.358 --> 01:20:33.258
- Ma'am?
- Find out where he's going.


01:20:33.360 --> 01:20:35.351
- He's on to something.
- Ma'am, the CIA is insisting...


01:20:35.429 --> 01:20:37.954
I could give a shit about the CIA
or their trumped-up evidence.


01:20:38.065 --> 01:20:41.057
He's my agent, and I trust him. Go on.


01:20:53.480 --> 01:20:56.210
- Get in.
- Are you gonna try and shoot me?


01:20:56.283 --> 01:20:57.875
I said, get in.


01:21:12.499 --> 01:21:15.059
You're gonna get botulism
if you keep drinking that.


01:21:15.135 --> 01:21:17.000
It's bottled water.


01:21:18.072 --> 01:21:20.802
It probably came from some stream
just around the corner from here.


01:21:20.908 --> 01:21:23.433
Bunch of little kids peeing in it.


01:21:24.612 --> 01:21:26.079
That's why I eat the peppers.


01:21:26.146 --> 01:21:31.243
Well, all I'm saying is
you can't trust a damn thing around here.


01:21:37.591 --> 01:21:39.991
You know,
you should just answer, "CIA," Felix.


01:21:40.094 --> 01:21:42.392
A taxi driver told me
where the office was.


01:21:42.463 --> 01:21:46.661
Well, if we're so easy to find, James,
you really should come visit.


01:21:47.768 --> 01:21:51.397
Or maybe you should come out
and see some more of the city.


01:22:11.358 --> 01:22:13.292
I heard a rumor you'd gone native.


01:22:13.360 --> 01:22:14.622
Felix.


01:22:19.800 --> 01:22:22.030
You know, I was just wondering
what South America would look like


01:22:22.136 --> 01:22:24.297
if nobody gave a damn
about coke or communism.


01:22:24.371 --> 01:22:26.965
It's always impressed me the way
you boys have carved this place up.


01:22:27.041 --> 01:22:30.169
I'll take that as a compliment
coming from a Brit.


01:22:31.712 --> 01:22:34.806
Are you sure you're playing
with the right side?


01:22:34.882 --> 01:22:36.816
Regimes change once a week down here.


01:22:36.884 --> 01:22:38.784
Medrano'll be no dirtier
than the next guy.


01:22:38.852 --> 01:22:40.877
Oh, you see, that's what I
like about U.S. intelligence.


01:22:40.988 --> 01:22:42.387
You'll lie down with anybody.


01:22:42.489 --> 01:22:44.889
Including you, brother. Including you.


01:22:44.992 --> 01:22:47.392
Do you know you're being played?


01:22:47.494 --> 01:22:49.223
Dominic Greene's gonna
suck this place dry,


01:22:49.330 --> 01:22:50.797
and then he's gonna move on,
and you're gonna be left


01:22:50.864 --> 01:22:52.126
picking up the broken crockery.


01:22:52.199 --> 01:22:55.066
What can I tell you?
There's no such thing as a free lunch.


01:22:55.169 --> 01:22:57.069
Well, you see, Felix,
I don't think you're half as cynical


01:22:57.171 --> 01:22:58.297
as you make out to be.


01:22:58.372 --> 01:23:00.169
You don't know me.


01:23:02.676 --> 01:23:05.543
Why? Just because you didn't come alone?


01:23:06.180 --> 01:23:08.648
- How long have I got?
- Thirty seconds.


01:23:10.517 --> 01:23:13.816
Well, that doesn't give us
a lot of time, does it?


01:23:14.855 --> 01:23:18.382
Medrano can't move until he pays off
the army and the police chief.


01:23:18.492 --> 01:23:20.084
<i>Greene's bringing
him his money now.</i>


01:23:20.194 --> 01:23:22.560
A hotel called La Perla de las Dunas


01:23:22.663 --> 01:23:24.187
in the desert.


01:23:24.732 --> 01:23:26.359
Thank you, Felix.


01:23:26.433 --> 01:23:28.526
James, move your ass.


01:23:29.703 --> 01:23:31.364
Get down! Get down, now!


01:23:46.720 --> 01:23:48.187
Move it! Move it!


01:23:54.528 --> 01:23:57.224
What the hell happened?
What did you tell him?


01:23:57.297 --> 01:23:59.265
Just what we agreed.


01:25:23.183 --> 01:25:25.014
What are you doing?


01:25:26.820 --> 01:25:28.685
The slide's caught.


01:25:29.656 --> 01:25:31.954
Maybe you should check your own.


01:25:32.025 --> 01:25:33.617
I will.


01:25:38.398 --> 01:25:40.628
Have you ever killed someone?


01:25:43.904 --> 01:25:46.202
Your training will tell you that
when the adrenaline kicks in


01:25:46.306 --> 01:25:48.137
you should compensate.


01:25:49.176 --> 01:25:53.806
But part of you is not gonna believe
the training because this kill is personal.


01:25:54.548 --> 01:25:56.379
Take a deep breath.


01:25:56.717 --> 01:25:58.480
You only need one shot.


01:25:58.552 --> 01:26:00.349
Make it count.


01:27:07.120 --> 01:27:08.417
In euros,


01:27:09.389 --> 01:27:10.788
as requested.


01:27:10.891 --> 01:27:13.519
The dollar isn't what it once was.


01:27:14.561 --> 01:27:16.290
The cost of war.


01:27:18.031 --> 01:27:20.625
I am afraid that the corruption
in this current government


01:27:20.734 --> 01:27:22.964
can no longer be tolerated.


01:27:25.772 --> 01:27:27.069
And mine?


01:27:27.774 --> 01:27:30.436
Right after you sign over my land.


01:27:46.093 --> 01:27:48.084
My first official act.


01:27:53.500 --> 01:27:55.764
And this, if you would.


01:27:55.836 --> 01:27:57.167
What is this?


01:27:57.271 --> 01:27:58.431
As of this moment,


01:27:58.505 --> 01:28:03.499
my organization owns
more than 60% of Bolivia's water supply.


01:28:03.610 --> 01:28:07.273
So this contract states
that your new government


01:28:07.347 --> 01:28:10.282
will use us as utilities provider.


01:28:11.084 --> 01:28:14.019
This is double what we are paying now.


01:28:17.591 --> 01:28:19.786
Well, then don't sign it.


01:28:20.527 --> 01:28:25.123
But you should know something
about me and the people I work with.


01:28:26.266 --> 01:28:28.291
<i>We deal with the
left or the right,</i>


01:28:28.368 --> 01:28:31.997
with dictators or liberators.


01:28:32.639 --> 01:28:35.267
If the current president
had been more agreeable,


01:28:35.342 --> 01:28:37.537
I wouldn't be talking to you.


01:28:37.644 --> 01:28:39.874
So, if you decide not to sign,


01:28:39.980 --> 01:28:42.141
you will wake up
with your balls in your mouth


01:28:42.215 --> 01:28:45.548
and your willing replacement
standing over you.


01:28:47.387 --> 01:28:49.685
If you doubt that, then shoot me,


01:28:49.790 --> 01:28:53.021
<i>take that money
and have a good night's sleep.</i>


01:29:53.387 --> 01:29:55.855
You and I had a mutual friend.


01:32:45.892 --> 01:32:48.827
Sounds like you just lost another one.


01:33:58.298 --> 01:34:00.493
Not this way. Not this way.


01:34:01.134 --> 01:34:03.125
I can't. I can't.


01:34:14.314 --> 01:34:15.645
Come here.


01:34:20.754 --> 01:34:22.517
Like you said,


01:34:22.622 --> 01:34:24.487
"Take a deep breath.


01:34:25.759 --> 01:34:27.351
"Make it count."


01:34:33.500 --> 01:34:35.263
Close your eyes.


01:34:43.777 --> 01:34:45.108
Come on!


01:34:59.626 --> 01:35:01.150
Wait here.


01:35:33.059 --> 01:35:35.857
- You promised that you'd...
- Let you go?


01:35:36.396 --> 01:35:38.728
I answered your questions.


01:35:38.832 --> 01:35:41.562
I told you what you wanted
to know about Quantum.


01:35:41.668 --> 01:35:43.192
Yes, you did,


01:35:43.570 --> 01:35:46.539
and your friends'd know that
so they're probably looking for you.


01:35:46.706 --> 01:35:50.335
But the good news is,
you're in the middle of a desert.


01:35:54.080 --> 01:35:55.377
Here.


01:35:57.250 --> 01:36:00.947
I bet you make it 20 miles before you
consider drinking that.


01:36:01.054 --> 01:36:02.954
Goodbye, Mr. Greene.


01:36:42.629 --> 01:36:44.096
Thank you.


01:36:44.831 --> 01:36:46.799
It's my pleasure.


01:36:47.934 --> 01:36:49.561
Are you all right?


01:36:49.969 --> 01:36:51.163
Fine.


01:36:51.638 --> 01:36:53.970
But I keep thinking, "He's dead.


01:36:54.407 --> 01:36:55.772
"Now what?"


01:36:56.242 --> 01:36:58.676
Well, the dam we saw
will have to come down,


01:36:58.778 --> 01:36:59.802
and there'll be others, too.


01:36:59.913 --> 01:37:02.780
Someone who worked for Greene
might be of help.


01:37:03.650 --> 01:37:05.481
Not a bad idea.


01:37:10.089 --> 01:37:12.990
Do you think they'll
be able to sleep now?


01:37:15.361 --> 01:37:18.353
I don't think the dead
care about vengeance.


01:37:20.800 --> 01:37:22.995
I wish I could set you free.


01:37:27.440 --> 01:37:29.601
But your prison is in there.


01:38:20.894 --> 01:38:23.328
Fine. Anything for an easy life.


01:38:26.833 --> 01:38:28.232
Sit down.


01:38:28.968 --> 01:38:30.333
Sit down!


01:38:31.671 --> 01:38:33.229
It's okay, baby.


01:38:50.089 --> 01:38:51.716
You're Canadian?


01:38:52.258 --> 01:38:54.658
You work in Canadian intelligence?


01:38:54.727 --> 01:38:56.922
It's all right. I know you do.


01:38:57.430 --> 01:38:59.330
And knowing this man,


01:38:59.399 --> 01:39:01.924
I'd guess you have access
to some very sensitive material


01:39:02.035 --> 01:39:04.094
which you're gonna be forced to give up.


01:39:04.203 --> 01:39:05.363
His life will be threatened,


01:39:05.438 --> 01:39:08.407
and because you love him,
you won't hesitate.


01:39:09.375 --> 01:39:11.366
It's a beautiful necklace.


01:39:12.078 --> 01:39:14.012
Did he give it to you?


01:39:15.915 --> 01:39:18.110
I have one just like it.


01:39:20.954 --> 01:39:23.422
He gave it to a friend of mine,


01:39:23.523 --> 01:39:25.457
someone very close to me.


01:39:29.228 --> 01:39:30.559
Your name is?


01:39:30.630 --> 01:39:32.359
- Corrine.
- Corrine.


01:39:32.966 --> 01:39:34.456
Corrine, I suggest you leave now.


01:39:34.567 --> 01:39:37.035
You contact your people,
and you tell them to check their seals.


01:39:37.103 --> 01:39:38.934
They have a leak.


01:39:39.038 --> 01:39:40.801
Do it now, please.


01:39:41.741 --> 01:39:44.767
This man and I have
some unfinished business.


01:39:55.421 --> 01:39:56.786
Thank you.


01:40:01.461 --> 01:40:02.723
Please.


01:40:03.429 --> 01:40:04.987
Make it quick.


01:40:14.340 --> 01:40:15.807
Is he still alive?


01:40:15.908 --> 01:40:17.102
He is.


01:40:17.610 --> 01:40:19.168
I'm surprised.


01:40:20.346 --> 01:40:22.177
Did you find what you were looking for?


01:40:22.281 --> 01:40:23.680
- Yes.
- Good.


01:40:25.118 --> 01:40:28.087
- I assume you have no regrets.
- I don't.


01:40:28.154 --> 01:40:29.849
What about you?


01:40:30.256 --> 01:40:33.157
Of course not.
That would be unprofessional.


01:40:34.127 --> 01:40:35.185
They found Greene dead


01:40:35.294 --> 01:40:38.024
in the middle of the Bolivian desert,
of all places.


01:40:38.131 --> 01:40:40.531
Two bullets in the back of his skull.


01:40:40.633 --> 01:40:43.329
They found motor oil in his stomach.


01:40:43.436 --> 01:40:45.370
Does that mean anything to you?


01:40:45.471 --> 01:40:47.098
Wish I could help.


01:40:47.173 --> 01:40:50.199
You'll be glad to know, I straightened
things out with the Americans.


01:40:50.309 --> 01:40:52.174
Your friend Leiter's been promoted.


01:40:52.278 --> 01:40:53.643
He replaced Beam.


01:40:53.713 --> 01:40:56.181
Well, then the right
people kept their jobs.


01:40:56.282 --> 01:40:58.011
Something like that.


01:40:59.552 --> 01:41:02.112
Congratulations. You were right.


01:41:02.188 --> 01:41:03.621
About what?


01:41:04.190 --> 01:41:05.782
About Vesper.


01:41:08.161 --> 01:41:09.492
Ma'am.


01:41:11.798 --> 01:41:13.060
Bond,


01:41:14.400 --> 01:41:16.129
I need you back.


01:41:16.536 --> 01:41:18.026
I never left.


01:43:18.027 --> 01:43:19.027
Subtitles by LeapinLar

